\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=201 valign=top style='width:150.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='line-height:115%'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>D-DIMER,\r\n  Plasma<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=107 valign=top style='width:80.25pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Times-New-Roman-Bold'>0.32<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=93 valign=top style='width:69.75pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Times-New-Roman'>mg\/L<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=346 valign=top style='width:259.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.6pt;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n  <\/span><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n  Times-New-Roman'>&lt; 0.50<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=201 valign=top style='width:150.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='line-height:115%'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>(Immunofluorescence\r\n  Method)<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=107 valign=top style='width:80.25pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=93 valign=top style='width:69.75pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=346 valign=top style='width:259.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.6pt;line-height:115%'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Note:<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>1. Degree of D-dimer increase\r\ndoes not definitely correlate with clinical severity of associated disease\r\nstate.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2. Increase levels have a high\r\nprobability of Venous thrombolism (VTE) and require clinical correlation.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3. Lipemia falsely decrease\r\nD-dimer levels.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>4.\r\nTest conducted on Citrated plasma.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Comments<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>D-dimer is one of the measurable\r\nhyproducts of activated of the fibrinolytic system. It assesses fibrinlytic\r\nactivation and<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>intravascular thrombosis. D-dimer\r\nassays are characteristic for Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)as\r\nthis test<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>demonstrates simultaneous\r\npresence of thrombin and plasmin formation. It can also be elevated in\r\nindividuals with large<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>vessel thrombosis, soft tissue\r\nhematomas, Pulmonary embolism, recent surgery, active or recent bleeding,\r\npregnancy, liver<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>disease, malignancy and\r\nhypercoagulable states. D-dimer is of particular value in excluding the\r\ndiagnosis of venous<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>thrombolism among patients at\r\nhigh risk.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>The\r\nResults relate to the sample tested only<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"153.0pt 45.0pt 72.0pt 42.55pt"}}